      "query": "So I've been reading through a bunch of project management material lately and I keep getting confused about the monitoring and controlling process group versus the executing process group, especially when it comes to risk \u2014 like, I understand you identify risks up front during planning, but I'm not totally clear on what actually happens to those risks once the project is underway and things start changing, new risks pop up that nobody planned for, existing risks either go away or turn out to be worse than expected, and someone has to keep track of all of that continuously rather than just once \u2014 can you explain, in the context of this document, what risk monitoring actually involves day to day?",
